What Are Gasoline Small Engines?
Gasoline small engines represent the workhorses of portable power generation, converting chemical energy from gasoline into mechanical power through internal combustion. Typically featuring displacements between 50cc-1000cc, these compact powerplants deliver exceptional power-to-weight ratios through their simple yet durable designs utilizing intake, compression, combustion, and exhaust cycles. Their versatility makes them indispensable for:

Landscaping equipment (riding mowers, chainsaws)
Construction tools (generators, concrete saws)
Agricultural implements (tillers, pumps)
Small vehicles (motorcycles, utility task vehicles)
